Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.merthyr.gov.uk/ieListDocuments.aspx?CId=222&MId=6893"},{"date":"2026-12-16","committee":"Cabinet","time":"4.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.merthyr.gov.uk/ieListDocuments.aspx?CId=160&MId=6841"},{"date":"2026-12-16","committee":"Full Council","time":"5.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.merthyr.gov.uk/ieListDocuments.aspx?CId=159&MId=6853"},{"date":"2027-01-11","committee":"Scrutiny: Aspirational Merthyr Tydfil","time":"4.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.merthyr.gov.uk/ieListDocuments.aspx?CId=521&MId=6873"},{"date":"2027-01-12","committee":"Scrutiny: Sustainable Merthyr Tydfil","time":"4.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.merthyr.gov.uk/ieListDocuments.aspx?CId=519&MId=6878"},{"date":"2027-01-18","committee":"Scrutiny: Healthier Merthyr Tydfil","time":"4.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.merthyr.gov.uk/ieListDocuments.aspx?CId=520&MId=6884"},{"date":"2027-01-19","committee":"Scrutiny: Thriving Merthyr Tydfil","time":"4.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.merthyr.gov.uk/ieListDocuments.aspx?CId=522&MId=6889"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-07-15","committee":"Full Council","time":"5.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.merthyr.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-14","committee":"Scrutiny: Aspirational Merthyr Tydfil","time":"4.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.merthyr.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-15","committee":"Scrutiny: Sustainable Merthyr Tydfil","time":"4.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.merthyr.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-21","committee":"Scrutiny: Healthier Merthyr Tydfil","time":"4.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.merthyr.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-22","committee":"Scrutiny: Thriving Merthyr Tydfil","time":"4.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.merthyr.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-28","committee":"Governance and Audit Committee","time":"5.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.merthyr.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-30","committee":"Cabinet","time":"4.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.merthyr.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-30","committee":"Full Council","time":"5.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.merthyr.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-22","committee":"Cabinet","time":"4.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.merthyr.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-22","committee":"Full Council","time":"5.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.merthyr.gov.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Merthyr Tydfil projects controllable earmarked reserves down from 15,694 to 9,599 by March 2027","lead":"Merthyr Tydfil council's papers for its Cabinet meeting on 22 October project that its controllable earmarked reserves, money set aside for named purposes, will fall from 15,694 on 31 March 2026 to 9,599 on 31 March 2027. Appendix 3 gives the figures as they appear in its table, without stating a unit in the material the desk reviewed.\n\nThe table shows the drop is steepest in 2026/27. The corporate part of those reserves is projected to fall from 11,674 on 31 March 2026 to 6,077 on 31 March 2027. The controllable total is then projected at 7,671 on 31 March 2028, 7,426 on 31 March 2029 and 7,348 on 31 March 2030.\n\nThe projection ends at 7,216 on 31 March 2031. The decline after March 2028 is much smaller than in the first year of the projection, with the total falling by 455 over the three years from March 2028 to March 2031.","iso":"2026-10-22","paper_title":"Appendix 3","paper_url":"https://democracy.merthyr.gov.uk/documents/s77199/77199.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-10-22","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Appendix 4","paper_url":"https://democracy.merthyr.gov.uk/documents/s77200/77200.pdf","headline":"\u00a3158k Hardship Funding \u2013 Supporting Digital Transformation reserve is proposed to be consolidated into the Transformation Programme Reserve","detail":"The paper proposes consolidating the \u00a3158k Hardship Funding reserve into the Transformation Programme Reserve. It says funds in the consolidated reserve can be borrowed by departments to fund invest-to-save schemes or transformation activity.","category":"reserves","matters":"Internal borrowing from a transformation reserve for invest-to-save schemes is a method a finance director may want to compare with their own approach to funding transformation.","figures":"\"158\" (\u00a3'000) for each of the Hardship Funding and Transformation Programme reserves.","quote":"EMR to be consolidated with Transformation Programme","read_on":"2026-10-19","material":false},{"iso":"2026-10-22","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Appendix 4","paper_url":"https://democracy.merthyr.gov.uk/documents/s77200/77200.pdf","headline":"\u00a3125k Levelling Up Fund capacity-building reserve, set up in 2023/24, is proposed for release as no longer required for its intended purpose","detail":"The paper says the reserve was set up in 2023/24 and is no longer required for its intended purpose, so the balance can be released. It is one of several reserves in Appendix 4 that the paper describes as no longer needed.","category":"reserves","matters":"A reserve set up for a specific grant-funded purpose being released shows how the council is clearing balances it no longer needs, which a peer or lender may compare with its own reserve reviews.","figures":"\"125\" (\u00a3'000) for the Levelling Up Fund capacity-building reserve.","quote":"EMR set up in 2023/24 and no longer required for the intended purpose.","read_on":"2026-10-19","material":false},{"iso":"2026-10-22","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Appendix 4","paper_url":"https://democracy.merthyr.gov.uk/documents/s77200/77200.pdf","headline":"\u00a3195k Redundancy Cost Reserve is proposed to fund the existing Retirement / Severance reserve","detail":"The Redundancy Cost Reserve, at \u00a3195k, is proposed to fund the existing Retirement / Severance reserve. The paper says this will support or offset the costs of employee severance revenue requirements.","category":"reserves","matters":"Severance costs are a recurring pressure in council budgets, and a finance director would want to see how they are funded from reserves rather than the revenue budget.","figures":"\"195\" (\u00a3'000) for the Redundancy Cost Reserve.","quote":"costs of employee severance revenue requirements.","read_on":"2026-10-19","material":false},{"iso":"2026-10-22","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Appendix 4","paper_url":"https://democracy.merthyr.gov.uk/documents/s77200/77200.pdf","headline":"\u00a3103k of the Efficiencies and Improvement Reserve is proposed for release to support the revenue budget","detail":"The paper proposes releasing part of the Efficiencies and Improvement Reserve to support the revenue budget. It states the aim is to reduce the 2027/28 annual budget's exposure to short-term financial volatility from one-off or time-limited items.","category":"reserves","matters":"Using a reserve to support the revenue budget is a direct draw on the council's cushion, and the stated purpose is to reduce the 2027/28 budget's exposure to volatility.","figures":"\"103\" (\u00a3'000) for the Efficiencies and Improvement Reserve.","quote":"Part of EMR to be released in order to support the Council\u2019s revenue budget","read_on":"2026-10-19","material":false},{"iso":"2026-10-22","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Appendix 4","paper_url":"https://democracy.merthyr.gov.uk/documents/s77200/77200.pdf","headline":"Appendix 4 proposes repurposing or releasing \u00a3506k across 13 earmarked reserves, with balances as at 31 March 2026","detail":"The table moves \u00a3506k from 13 earmarked reserves to new purposes or to release. The largest items are the Redundancy Cost Reserve (\u00a3195k) and the Hardship Funding and Transformation Programme reserves (\u00a3158k each). The paper also proposes \u00a3125k for the Elections Reserve to meet the May 2027 ordinary local elections.","category":"reserves","matters":"A finance director at another council, or a lender, would want to see how much one-off reserve cover is being moved into the revenue budget or into other uses in a single decision.","figures":"\u00a3'000 table; 13 reserves listed. Total row: \"TOTAL 506 506\" (From and To columns). Elections Reserve \"125\".","quote":"TOTAL 506","read_on":"2026-10-19","material":false}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-10-22"},"name":"Merthyr Tydfil","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-10-26","since_iso":"2026-09-26","distress":false,"headline":"\u00a3158k Hardship Funding \u2013 Supporting Digital Transformation reserve is proposed to be consolidated into the Transformation Programme Reserve","lead":"Internal borrowing from a transformation reserve for invest-to-save schemes is a method a finance director may want to compare with their own approach to funding transformation.","also":["26 other findings in this window","47 papers caught"],"watch":"Scrutiny: Thriving Merthyr Tydfil on 2026-11-17","n_findings":27,"n_documents":47,"top_paper_title":"Appendix 4","top_paper_url":"https://democracy.merthyr.gov.uk/documents/s77200/77200.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":56,"news_drafts_total":1}}